{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbeZQSbapLQzUrjdfs8s", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags in this project are plain booleans in a TOML file, read through one helper.\n\n**How it works**\n- `flags.toml` has a `[flags]` table. It currently contains one flag, `invoice-pdf-v2 = false`.\n- `src/flags.py` loads that file once, at import time. `flags.is_on(\"name\")` returns the flag's boolean value.\n- `is_on` returns `False` for any name that isn't in the file. A typo in a flag name therefore fails silently and leaves the flag off. It does not raise an error.\n- `all_flags()` returns a copy of the whole table.\n- There are no per-user, per-environment or percentage rollouts. A flag is either on or off for everyone.\n\n**Conventions** (from a stored project memory, which matches the code)\n- Read flags only through `flags.is_on(\"name\")`.\n- Flag names are kebab-case.\n- Every flag must be declared in `flags.toml`.\n\n**For the new checkout flow**\n1. Add a line to `flags.toml`, for example `checkout-v2 = false`. The name is only an example.\n2. Branch in the checkout code with `if flags.is_on(\"checkout-v2\"): ...`. Keep the old path as the `else` branch.\n3. Flip the value to `true` in `flags.toml` to enable it.\n\nBecause the file is read at import, changing it needs a restart or redeploy to take effect. I didn't look for existing checkout code or tests. If you'd like, I can add the flag and wire up the branch."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 440, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25366, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 440}, "output_tokens": 488, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "sess